    "title": "Singapore 2024 port delay: a constructed SME replenishment decision",
    "data_status": "Public event context; all orders, prices, rates and option timings are constructed assumptions.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "mpa_20240530",
        "title": "MPA response on extended waiting times, 30 May 2024",
        "url": "https://www.mpa.gov.sg/media-centre/details/in-response-to-media-queries-on--vessels--extended-waiting-times-for-berths-in-the-port-of-singapore",
        "published": "2024-05-30",
        "accessed": "2026-10-04",
        "facts": [
          "MPA linked off-schedule arrivals and vessel bunching to upstream disruptions and Cape of Good Hope diversions.",
          "Most container vessels berthed on arrival. Where schedule adjustment was infeasible, average waiting was about 2–3 days.",
          "January–April 2024 container throughput was 13.36 million TEU, up 8.8% year on year.",
          "Additional resources raised stated weekly handling capacity from 770,000 to 820,000 TEU."
        ],
        "not_supported": "This statement does not provide shipment-level arrival observations, a delay probability distribution, freight quotes or insurance rates."
      },
      {
        "id": "tradetrust_20230825",
        "title": "TradeTrust Singapore–India trade-finance transaction, 25 August 2023",
        "url": "https://www.tradetrust.io/happenings-and-resources/press-release-singapore-india-kick-off-interoperable-ebills-of-lading-for-trade-finance/",
        "published": "2023-08-25",
        "accessed": "2026-10-04",
        "facts": [
          "The documented physical shipment was scrap metal from Miami to Gujarat.",
          "DBS, ICICI Bank, traders and Maersk participated in a paperless eBL and letter-of-credit workflow with documentary checks and title transfers."
        ],
        "not_supported": "HarborShield has no access to those transaction documents and no bank, TradeTrust or eBL title-transfer integration."
      }
    ],
